cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SPDF in your work, please cite the specification, with the
  version you used.
title: "SPDF: Semantic Processed Document Format, version 5.0"
abstract: >-
  SPDF is an open, portable file format for documents that have been read
  once and can be cited forever. A .spdf file is a single uncompressed
  SQLite 3 database that holds one document (a printed book, a scan, a
  recording, a slide deck, a spreadsheet or a web page) as citable units and
  searchable fragments. Every fragment carries an exact anchor: the printed
  page or leaf, the verse, the canonical reference, the second of a
  recording or the slide, with a portable anchor URI aligned with W3C Media
  Fragments and RFC 5147. Metadata is a CSL-JSON item, full-text search uses
  the tokenizers that ship with SQLite, optional embedding vectors from
  several models can live side by side, and content can be hashed and signed
  with Ed25519. A public conformance suite defines the expected behaviour of
  every implementation. This is the working draft of version 5.0.
